   <text:p text:style-name="P45"><text:span text:style-name="T25">Moringa</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15">is often called a ‘</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T31">M</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">iracle </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T31">T</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T24">ree</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15">’ because it is considered effective in combating global warming due to its growth and ability to absorb carbon dioxide </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T16">at 50 times faster than cedar trees</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15">. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T25">Moringa</text:span> can be consumed in many forms including:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="L1">
    <text:list-item>
