      </draw:frame>ge</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52">Powder can be substituted for 20% <text:span text:style-name="T43">of the wheat</text:span> in bread or pizza crust recipes</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52">Curry: <text:s/>fresh Moringa leaves, onion, tomato, curry, coconut milk, vegetables, chicken, rice</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52">Egg Scramble: eggs, Moringa powder, butter, salt</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P53">Energy Balls: oats, peanut butter, honey, Moringa powder, nuts, raisins </text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57"><text:span text:style-name="T25"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57"><text:span text:style-name="T25">Moringa</text:span> in the food industry:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="L7">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P58">Moringa can replace 20% of wheat flour in breads and pastas</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P58">Moringa can be added to many sauces</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P58">Course Shredded Dried Leaves can be substituted for tobacco for a healthy smoke</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54">Industrial uses of <text:span text:style-name="T25">Moringa</text:span>:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="L5">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P55">Seeds are used in water treatment plants to clean contaminents</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
